@NAME@
JewCal, a pixel-art Jewish calendar for the GeekMagic SmallTV Ultra (ESP8266)

!! FOR THE SMALLTV *ULTRA*: the stock firmware calls itself "Ultra-V9.x" and
!! its web page shows "Model: SmallTV-Ultra". For the SmallTV Pro (ESP32,
!! touch pad on top) use the other JewCal release (jewcal-pro-<version>.zip).

FILES
  jewcal-ultra-installer.bin  Step 1. Small enough for the stock firmware's
                              updater, whose space is limited (~500 KB).
  jewcal-ultra.bin            Step 2, and every later update.
  jewcal-ultra.elf            Debug symbols: decode a crash address with
                              xtensa-lx106-elf-addr2line -e jewcal-ultra.elf 0x4020....
  SHA256SUMS                  Checksums of the files above.

INSTALL (over WiFi: no cable, no opening the case)
  1. Find the SmallTV's address: the stock firmware shows it on its screen.
  2. Open http://<that address>/update in a browser (the stock web page's
     firmware update), choose jewcal-ultra-installer.bin and upload it.
     The SmallTV restarts into the JewCal installer.
  3. The installer's screen says where to go next. Either open
     http://<address>/ on your network (if the stock firmware's WiFi was
     remembered), or join the open WiFi network JEWCAL-INSTALL-XXXX and open
     http://192.168.4.1/.
  4. Choose jewcal-ultra.bin and Install. After about half a minute JewCal
     starts. It joins the network the stock firmware used.
  5. If the screen shows SETUP instead: join the WiFi network JEWCAL-XXXX
     from a phone, open http://192.168.4.1/ and pick your network.
  6. Open http://jewcal.local/ (or the address on JewCal's info screen) and
     choose your city. Done.

UPDATES
  Open http://jewcal.local/, click "Update firmware" at the bottom (its
  address changes at every restart, so other web pages cannot reach it) and
  upload the new jewcal-ultra.bin. Settings are kept.
  From a source checkout: make ultra-ota HOST=jewcal.local

FORGET THE WIFI NETWORK
  The Ultra has no button: use "Forget WiFi" at the bottom of the settings
  page. JewCal restarts into SETUP (step 5). It also opens SETUP by itself
  when the saved network cannot be joined.

BACK TO THE STOCK FIRMWARE
  GeekMagic publishes it at https://github.com/GeekMagicClock/smalltv-ultra
  (folders Ultra-V9.x.x, a zip with one .bin). Upload that .bin through
  "Update firmware" on JewCal's settings page. Photos stored by the stock
  firmware may be gone.

IF SOMETHING GOES WRONG
  * SAFE MODE on the screen: JewCal crashed 3 times in a row. Open the
    address on the screen: the page shows the last error and links to the
    update page, or restarts JewCal.
  * A SmallTV that does not start at all can only be rewritten through the
    serial pads inside (remove the 2 screws underneath; 3.3 V USB-UART
    adapter on 3V3/GND/TXD0/RXD0; hold GPIO0 to GND while powering on):
      esptool.py --chip esp8266 write_flash 0x0 jewcal-ultra.bin

Times come from Hebcal for the chosen location; ask your rabbi about local
customs. Calendar data: Hebcal.com. Weather data: Open-Meteo.com. Both CC BY 4.0.
